  "contentPlaintext": "<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\">PROJECT PLAN</textStyle></bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\">Course Assignment:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\"> [Insert Course Name / Code]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\">Project Group Name:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\"> Group [Insert Group Number / Letter]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\">Document Version:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\"> 1.0.0-Planning Baseline</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\">Date of Creation:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\"> May 28, 2026</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\">Faculty / Instructor:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"28pt\"> [Insert Instructor Name]</textStyle>\n<bold>Team Assignments & Contact Log</bold>\nName\nRole\nCore Responsibility Area\nInstitutional Email\n<italic>[Student 1]</italic>\nTeam Lead (Manager)\nTask Coordination / Integration\n<link class=\"text-teal-600 hover:underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"mailto:student1@faculty.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">student1@faculty.edu</link>\n<italic>[Student 2]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nTechnical Writing / Front-End\n<link class=\"text-teal-600 hover:underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"mailto:student2@faculty.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">student2@faculty.edu</link>\n<italic>[Student 3]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nBack-End / Logic Infrastructure\n<link class=\"text-teal-600 hover:underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"mailto:student3@faculty.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">student3@faculty.edu</link>\n<italic>[Student 4]</italic>\nStudent (Member)\nTesting Setup / Report Assembly\n<link class=\"text-teal-600 hover:underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"mailto:student4@faculty.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">student4@faculty.edu</link>\n<bold>Course Instructor Alignment Check</bold>\nEvaluator Assignment\nProject Status Profile\nAssigned Feedback / Comments\nReview Date\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Course Instructor</textStyle></bold>\n[ ] Plan Validated [ ] Revisions Required\n[Insert Instructor Notes]\n[Date]\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Project Scope & Functional Overview\n2.1 Project Core Concept\n2.2 Target Solution Summary\n3. Task Allocation & Responsibility Mapping\n3.1 Core Module Division\n4. Milestone Timeline & Assignment Deadlines\n4.1 Graded Deliverables Schedule\n5. Communication Plan & Workspace Rules\n5.1 Interaction Frequency Syncs\n5.2 Submission Review Procedures\n<bold>2. Project Scope & Functional Overview</bold>\n<bold>2.1 Project Core Concept</bold>\n<italic>[Provide a clear 150-word summary describing your group project. State the specific real-world problem you are trying to solve and outline the functional components your team will design and build to satisfy the course assignment rubric.]</italic>\n<bold>2.2 Target Solution Summary</bold>\nThe project team will build an application designed to address gaps in current technical setups. The system will prioritize clean interfaces, modular integration, and simple database structures. This approach ensures all requirements set out by the course instructor are delivered successfully before the final deadline.\n<bold>3. Task Allocation & Responsibility Mapping</bold>\n<bold>3.1 Core Module Division</bold>\nTo maintain high performance and balance workloads, the project is divided into distinct, manageable modules:\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Module 1 (Project Planning & Design Documentation):</textStyle></bold> Led by [Student 1] with design support from [Student 2]. Focuses on requirements gathering, component wireframing, and building UML architecture models.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Module 2 (Core Logic Implementation):</textStyle></bold> Led by [Student 3]. Focuses on setting up API loops, database persistence tables, and data sanitization layers.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Module 3 (User Interface Construction):</textStyle></bold> Led by [Student 2]. Focuses on building responsive layout frames and connecting inputs directly to backend service paths.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Module 4 (Verification & Quality Checking):</textStyle></bold> Led by [Student 4]. Focuses on writing system assertion checks, testing code execution stability, and organizing final reports.\n<bold>4. Milestone Timeline & Assignment Deadlines</bold>\n<bold>4.1 Graded Deliverables Schedule</bold>\nThe team will use 2-week internal planning intervals to keep work aligned with course milestone checkpoints:\nProject Phase\nGraded Faculty Deliverable\nTarget Functional Focus\nSubmission Deadline\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Phase 1</textStyle></bold>\nProject Plan\nInitial group alignment, team commitments, and task distribution.\n[Insert Date]\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Phase 2</textStyle></bold>\nRequirements Document (SRS)\nDefining system scope, identifying target users, and cataloging use cases.\n[Insert Date]\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Phase 3</textStyle></bold>\nDesign Document (RDD)\nBuilding database tables, mapping data flows, and defining API interfaces.\n[Insert Date]\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Phase 4</textStyle></bold>\nFinal Report & Software Bundle\nHanding over source files, running project walkthroughs, and final grading.\n[Insert Date]\n<bold>5. Communication Plan & Workspace Rules</bold>\n<bold>5.1 Interaction Frequency Syncs</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Internal Progress Syncs:</textStyle></bold> The group will meet twice a week using online communication tools to check task boards and resolve code blockages.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">General Group Workspace Notifications:</textStyle></bold> All project discussions will take place in dedicated team channels. Members must review updates and acknowledge messages within <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">24 hours</textStyle></bold>. [1]\n<bold>5.2 Submission Review Procedures</bold>\nBefore any official document moves to submission status, it must undergo a mandatory team review. The Team Lead checks the text against grading parameters, confirms code quality standards are met, and manages file transfers into the student portal.",
